  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 146 PM EDT Sat Aug 22 2026\n\nMainly dry conditions continue into early next week. Monday looks \nlike a beautiful day, with relatively low humidity and afternoon \nhighs in the low to mid 80s. A weak mid-level shortwave trough \nzipping through NW flow will move over the region late Monday. \nHowever, a sfc warm front is forecast to set up to our southwest and \nkeep higher rain chances focused across portions of MO, AR, and TN. \nHighs on Tuesday should reach the mid 80s. \n\nThe latest model guidance pushes a warm front a little further north \ninto central KY by Wednesday. With the development of broad upper \nlevel troughing, this could be enough for isolated to scattered \nshowers and storms Wednesday afternoon and evening. An upper level \ntrough continues to amplify in tandem with a sfc low across the \nGreat Lakes heading into Thursday. This system should drag a cold \nfront through the region on Thursday, bringing at least a small \nchance (20-30%) for showers and thunderstorms.   \n\nHighs in the mid and upper 80s will be common Wednesday through the \nend of the forecast period. A few of our warmer spots may touch 90 \non Wednesday and Thursday ahead of the cold front.",
